sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant B as Browser
    participant G as Gateway
    participant I as identity-service
    participant K as Kafka
    participant N as notification-service
    participant M as Mail / WhatsApp
    participant X as Google

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over U,M: Forgot password
    U->>B: enters email
    B->>G: POST /api/auth/forgot-password
    G->>I: forward
    I->>I: human check, then find account (answer is always 200)
    I->>I: make 6-digit code, store only its hash, life 2 h
    I->>K: notification.requested (code)
    K->>N: consume
    N->>M: email through the outbox
    U->>B: code + new password
    B->>G: POST /api/auth/reset-password
    G->>I: forward
    I->>I: code single use, password policy, revoke all sessions
    I-->>B: password reset
    end

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over U,X: Sign in with Google
    U->>B: Continue with Google
    B->>X: Google sign-in
    X-->>B: ID token
    B->>G: POST /api/auth/google {idToken}
    G->>I: forward
    I->>X: verify the token
    X-->>I: verified email
    I->>I: existing account, or create a STUDENT only if self-registration is on
    I-->>B: access + refresh (same as password login)
    end

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over U,M: Sign in with a WhatsApp code
    B->>G: POST /api/auth/whatsapp/request-code
    G->>I: forward
    I->>M: send one-time code (always answers 200)
    U->>B: code
    B->>G: POST /api/auth/whatsapp/verify
    G->>I: forward
    I-->>B: access + refresh
    end
